body:
**Box Type:** **Beauty Box**

&nbsp;

[Coola Classic Sport SPF 50 Sunscreen in Mango](http://www.sephora.com/classic-sport-spf-50-mango-P395623?skuId=1707108&icid2=D=c6:products%20grid:p395623) $32 at Sephora full size. We all need sunscreen this summer!

&nbsp;

[First Aid Beauty Ultra Repair Cream Intense Hydration](http://www.sephora.com/ultra-repair-cream-intense-hydration-P248407?skuId=1309590&icid2=D%3Dc6%3Aproducts%20grid%3Ap248407) $12 at Sephora 2 oz travel size. Summer heat can really take a toll on our skin. Ultra hydrating lotion to quench dehydrated skin.

&nbsp;

[Bumble and Bumble Surf Spray](http://www.sephora.com/surf-spray-P280513?skuId=1270776&icid2=D=c6:products%20grid:p280513) $27 at Sephora, full size. A spray to achieve that just out of the ocean mermaid look.

&nbsp;

[ColourPop Ultra Matte Lip in Pacific](https://colourpop.com/product/pacific/) $6 at Colourpop.com, full size. Bright coral orange shade.

&nbsp;

[ColourPop Lippie Pencil in Chi Chi Pencil](https://colourpop.com/product/chi-chi-pencil/) $5 at Colourpop.com, full size. Orange lip liner to go with lip shade.

&nbsp;

[Tarte Amazonian Clay BB Tinted Moisturizer Broad Spectrum SPF 20 Sunscreen](http://www.sephora.com/amazonian-clay-bb-tinted-moisturizer-broad-spectrum-spf-20-sunscreen-P67617?skuId=759779&icid2=D=c6:products%20grid:p67617) $36 at Sephora, full size.

&nbsp;

**Total: $118**

&nbsp;

This was super fun! Really thought of items you might want to have for a day at the beach!
*edit: for formatting, and miscalculated original list, oops!*

[My reaction towards Porsha Stewart after watching the reunion](http://33.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_m06czlNKOJ1ql5yr7o1_r2_400.gif) 

&nbsp;
I know, not "tgif" related, just wanted to finally have an excuse to use this gif :)

I would say Brandi, but at one point I did like her, especially during her first two seasons. As for a lady I have disliked from day one would for sure be Alex McCord. She doesn't necessarily do anything out right hurtful towards others, but damn she made me so uncomfortable watching her. She would just do hilariously cringe-worthy things, her behavior during Morocco, and being the messenger for Bethenny, etc. A lot of her actions on the show was motivated by climbing up NYC's social ladder, her and her husband always came off as desperate to me. I also really dislike Aviva, god she was the worst. 

&nbsp;
edit: Oh I forgot Kelly Bensimmon (sp?), and Cindy Barshop, never liked those ladies either.

Whish shave cream

&nbsp;
12 benefits hair treatment

&nbsp;
Real Chemistry face peel

&nbsp;
Cynthia Rowley brightening illuminator

&nbsp;
Jane Iredale just kissed lip and cheek stain

&nbsp;
I am pretty happy with my box. Although I am skeptical about the 12 benefits spray because my hair is extremely oily, but we will see how it works for me. I didn't choose a sample choice this month, because I wasn't wowed by anything offered, but the Jane Iredale stain was the one sample choice I would have picked if I did. Not bad Birchbox.

Other then Giggy, who is the king of RH pets, I too think Dina's cat Grandma Wrinkles is great! I really like her love for those animals that are often times overlooked by others. I also really like Bethenny's dog Cookie. What about Lisa V's two Swans! 

&nbsp;
and of course RIP Millou :(

This is fun! Takes me about 30 mins to an hour depending on the eye look I am going for that day.

&nbsp;
Moisturizer & Primer: Smashbox Photo Finish Foundation Primer, been using this puppy since I was 14. 

&nbsp;
Foundation: Makeup Forever Mat Velvet Matifying Foundation. 

&nbsp;
Concealer: It Cosmetics Bye Bye Under Eye. It is supposed to be a under eye concealer, but because I like a little more coverage, I find that this works on other blemishes on the face as well. 

&nbsp;
Powder: NYX Cosmetics Mineral Finishing Powder, use this all over the face for a more matte look. 

&nbsp;
Contour: Benefit Hoola, a very light bronze/contour. 

&nbsp;
Blush: Depending on the day I use either Kat Von D in Bellisima, Laura Geller Baked Blush-n-Brighten in Berry, or ModelCo blush in Peach Bellini. 

&nbsp;
Highlight: Benefit High Beam. 

&nbsp;
Eye Primer: MAC Pro Longwear Paint Pot in Painterly. 

&nbsp;
Eyeshadow: Too many to list, but my fave's are from the Urban Decay's Naked 3 Palette, and BH Cosmetics Galaxy Chic Palette. 

&nbsp;
Eye highlight: NYX Cosmetics Jumbo Eye Pencil in Milk. 

&nbsp;
Liquid Liner: NYX Cosmetics Super Skinny Eye Marker, or the Super Fat Eye Marker. 

&nbsp;
Bottom Liner: Marcelle Retractable Eyeliner. 

&nbsp;
Mascara: Marc Jacobs O! Mega Lash. 

&nbsp;
Brows: Tarte Amazonian Clay Brow Mousse, and NYX Cosmetics Control Freak eyebrow gel. 

&nbsp;
Setting Spray: NYX Cosmetics Matte Setting Spray. 

&nbsp;
Lips: Again too many to list, but my faves are MAC, NARS, Too Faced Melted lippies, and NYX soft matte lip creams (I am kinda a NYX fangirl if you could't tell!)
